From: Dmitry Baryshkov <dmitry.baryshkov@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-commit: 551468ad68b1854d914e5e2e2009af48a40b6ff4
Upstream: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/43896

ir3: report an unreachable register limit rather than assert

calc_limit_pressure_for_cs_with_barrier() can put the register limit below
what a shader needs, and spilling is then asked for something it cannot
deliver: the spiller only evicts values that are not live across the
instruction it is working on, so it can never get below that instruction's own
footprint, and it ends on an assertion in limit() instead of reporting
anything.  debugoptimized keeps asserts, and that is what CI builds.

Work out that floor first and fail the compile when the limit is under it.  A
workgroup whose waves all have to be resident at once cannot run at all in
that case, so there is nothing better to fall back to.

